{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>Is it realistic to think a couple can rebuild after this? The research is more hopeful than you might expect. Studies of affair recovery find that couples who commit to the work can improve to a place comparable with other couples in therapy (Atkins and colleagues). That is not a promise about your particular relationship, and it is not a reason to rush. It just means the door is not closed, even when it feels like it is.</p>
  <p>When a couple wants to move faster or go deeper than weekly sessions allow, a Couples Intensive, a focused four-to-eight-hour block in a single day, can do a lot of work at once. It's one of the ways this practice makes room for the harder cases. Ask about it on your free call. The dedicated page is on the way.</p>
